'''Windermere and Troutbeck (including Bridge House)''' is a [[National Trust for Places of Historic Interest or Natural Beauty|National Trust]] property consisting of land around [[Windermere]], a lake in [[Cumbria]], England.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Windermere and Troutbeck in windermere United Kingdom - reviews, best time to visit, photos of Windermere and Troutbeck, Family Holidays tours, things to do in windermere |url=https://www.hellotravel.com/united-kingdom/windermere-and-troutbeck |access-date=2024-02-25 |website=HelloTravel}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Windermere and Bowness {{!}} Cumbria County History Trust |url=https://www.cumbriacountyhistory.org.uk/township/windermere-and-bowness |access-date=2024-02-25 |website=www.cumbriacountyhistory.org.uk}}</ref>

This National Trust property includes the head of the Troutbeck Valley, several sites next to Windermere, and six farms. One of the farms &mdash; [[Troutbeck Park]] &mdash; once belonged to [[Beatrix Potter]] and was, in fact, her largest farm.<ref>{{Cite web |last=cumbriacom |date=2021-07-24 |title=Troutbeck |url=https://www.cumbria.com/troutbeck/ |access-date=2024-02-25 |website=Cumbria.com |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Visiting Troutbeck {{!}} Cumbria |url=https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/lake-district/townend/things-to-do-in-troutbeck |access-date=2024-02-25 |website=National Trust |language=en}}</ref>

Other popular places on the property include [[Ambleside Roman Fort]], Bridge House in [[Ambleside]], and Cockshott Point in [[Bowness-on-Windermere]].

